      "content": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nint A[1000][1000];\nint ps[1010][1010];\n\ntypedef long long ll;\n\nll solve(int m, int n, int k) {\n  const int d = min(m, n);\n  const int length = max(m, n);\n\n  // Each prefix boundary stores a contiguous vector along the longer axis.\n  fill(ps[0], ps[0] + length, 0);\n  if (m <= n) {\n    for (int b = 1; b <= d; b++) {\n      const int* previous = ps[b - 1];\n      const int* row = A[b - 1];\n      int* current = ps[b];\n      for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {\n        current[i] = previous[i] + row[i];\n      }\n    }\n  } else {\n    for (int b = 1; b <= d; b++) {\n      const int* previous = ps[b - 1];\n      int* current = ps[b];\n      for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {\n        current[i] = previous[i] + A[i][b - 1];\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  unordered_map<ll, ll> h;\n  ll ans = 0;\n  for (int first = 0; first < d; first++) {\n    const int* lower = ps[first];\n    for (int last = first + 1; last <= d; last++) {\n      const int* upper = ps[last];\n      h.clear();\n      h[0] = 1;\n      ll s = 0;\n      for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {\n        s += upper[i] - lower[i];\n        ans += h.find(s - k) != h.end() ? h[s - k] : 0;\n        h[s]++;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return ans;\n}\n\nint main() {\n  ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n  cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n  int k, m, n;\n  cin >> k >> m >> n;\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < m; i++)\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)\n      cin >> A[i][j];\n\n  cout << solve(m, n, k) << endl;\n  return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/main.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Pairing boundaries along the shorter dimension and scanning contiguous prefix vectors should improve locality and reduce enumeration work for wide matrices while preserving the reference frequency-counting kernel.",
